READING: near-tight families' witness phases ARE (near) an arithmetic {k*alpha} orbit
(low arith-defect, few gaps); loose families are NOT.  So M(near-tight) = the min-gap of a
{k*alpha} orbit = a continued-fraction convergent = an Ostrowski rung.  The gap is between rungs.
